    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Homeowners insurance in Utah covers a roof leak only if it is caused by a sudden, accidental, and covered peril.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "When Insurance Covers a Roof Leak"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Your policy typically pays for repairs to the roof and interior water damage if the leak results from:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Wind or hail storms (such as high winds tearing off shingles or severe hail cracking the roof)",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              1,
              2
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Falling objects (like a tree limb or debris crashing onto the roof)",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              1,
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Fire or lightning",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              1
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Heavy snow or ice weight (depending on policy terms, though structural collapse from weight is often covered)",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              4
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "When Insurance Does NOT Cover a Roof Leak"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Insurance companies will deny claims if the leak is caused by lack of upkeep or normal aging. Exclusions include:",
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Normal wear and tear (an old roof that simply reaches the end of its lifespan)",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              1
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Deferred maintenance (ignoring missing shingles, cracked flashing, or small known leaks for too long)",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              1
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Improper installation or poor workmanship",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              2
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Flooding or earthquakes (these require separate specialized policies or endorsements)",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              5
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "What You Should Do If You Have a Leak"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Mitigate further damage: Take reasonable steps to stop active water intrusion (such as placing a tarp or bucket), as failing to prevent extra damage can void coverage."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Document everything: Take clear photos and videos of the roof damage and any ruined interior ceilings, walls, or personal property."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Contact your insurance company: File a claim as soon as possible with your policy number. Do not sign a contract for a permanent replacement until an insurance adjuster has inspected the property."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Get help with disputes: If you run into a disagreement with your insurer over a claim settlement, you can reach out to the Utah Insurance Department at 801-957-9305 or 800-439-3805.",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "Utah Insurance Department",
                "link": "https://insurance.utah.gov/consumers/home-insurance/home-claims-info/"
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              5,
              6
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "To help narrow this down, can you tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What caused the leak (e.g., a recent wind/hail storm vs. old age)?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "How old the roof is?"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
